# Sample GRIB2 File

This is a placeholder for a sample GRIB2 file.

## Description

A sample GRIB2 file containing meteorological data for testing and demonstration purposes.

## Typical Contents

- Surface fields: 2m temperature, 10m wind components, surface pressure
- Pressure level fields: Temperature, geopotential, wind components
- Multiple time steps: Analysis and forecast steps
- Grid: Regular latitude-longitude grid

## File Size

Typical size: 1-10 MB depending on resolution and number of fields

## How to Obtain

Sample GRIB files can be obtained from:
- ECMWF Public Dataset: https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/datasets
- NCEP GFS: https://www.nco.ncep.noaa.gov/pmb/data/gfs/
- NOAA NOMADS: https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/

## Example Usage

```python
import eccodes

with open('sample_grib2.grib', 'rb') as f:
    msg_id = eccodes.codes_grib_new_from_file(f)
    
    shortName = eccodes.codes_get(msg_id, 'shortName')
    values = eccodes.codes_get_values(msg_id)
    
    print(f"Field: {shortName}")
    print(f"Number of values: {len(values)}")
    
    eccodes.codes_release(msg_id)
```

## Notes

- This is a text placeholder file
- Actual GRIB files are binary and cannot be represented as text
- Replace this file with an actual GRIB2 file for testing